WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.958 --> 00:00:11.375
Joey Lynn King was born on
July 30 1999 in Los Angeles.

00:00:11.458 --> 00:00:13.042
She began acting
professionally

00:00:13.125 --> 00:00:14.542
at the age of four,

00:00:14.625 --> 00:00:17.583
appearing in a commercial
for Life cereal in 2003,

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:20.542
as well as ads
for Kay jewellers in 2007

00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:22.750
and AT&amp;T in 2009.

00:00:22.833 --> 00:00:24.833
She even appeared
in a commercial for Eggos

00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:25.750
in 2005,

00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:27.708
proving she's not
the only Netflix star

00:00:27.792 --> 00:00:29.375
with a taste
for frozen waffles.

00:00:32.708 --> 00:00:33.875
In February 2006,

00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:35.958
she made
her first TV appearance

00:00:36.042 --> 00:00:37.875
in The Suite Life
of Zack &amp; Cody

00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:40.500
in which she appeared twice
as Emily Mason,

00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:42.792
a young girl who Zac
and Cody have to look after

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:44.667
when they get roped into
running a day care centre.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.042
Come on, horsey! Faster!

00:00:47.125 --> 00:00:49.542
King's film debut
followed in 2007

00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:50.833
in Reign Over Me,

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.667
in which she briefly
appeared as Gina,

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:55.333
the daughter of Adam
Sandler's character Charlie.

00:00:55.417 --> 00:00:56.333
The same year,

00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:58.417
she appeared in Entourage
episode "Gotcha!"

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.042
as the daughter of
UFC fighter Chuck Liddell,

00:01:01.125 --> 00:01:02.458
as well as two episodes of

00:01:02.542 --> 00:01:03.792
CSI:
Crime Scene Investigation,

00:01:03.875 --> 00:01:05.750
including
"Woulda, Coulda, Shoulda",

00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:08.000
where she plays the daughter
of a murdered woman

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:10.000
who holds the key
to the investigation.

00:01:10.083 --> 00:01:11.292
In 2008,

00:01:11.375 --> 00:01:13.292
she played the role
of Kelly Mackenzie

00:01:13.375 --> 00:01:15.917
in the season four finale
of "Medium" Drowned World.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.625
And she followed that
with the first of

00:01:17.708 --> 00:01:19.125
many voice-over jobs,

00:01:19.208 --> 00:01:21.750
playing the role of Katie,
an abnormal yellow yak

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:23.042
with frightening teeth,

00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:23.958
in Horton Hears a Who!

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:27.083
In my world,
everyone's a pony

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:30.417
and they all eat rainbows
and poop butterflies.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.667
In 2010,
she featured as Cassidy

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:33.958
in two episodes of
Ghost Whisperer

00:01:34.042 --> 00:01:36.167
and landed her biggest role
to date the same year,

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.500
playing the lead in
Elizabeth Allen's 2010 film

00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:41.958
Ramona and Beezus
alongside Selena Gomez.

00:01:42.542 --> 00:01:44.000
It's picture perfect, right?

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.125
Let's be realistic, Ramona.

00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:48.125
This is a curling iron,
not a magic wand.

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:49.667
King starred as Ramona,

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.000
an adventurous, imaginative
third grader

00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:54.042
whose attempts to solve her
family and friends' problems

00:01:54.125 --> 00:01:56.083
seem to backfire
spectacularly.

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.500
King also released a single
to accompany the movie

00:01:58.583 --> 00:01:59.792
called "Ramona Blue".

00:01:59.875 --> 00:02:01.792
Two more movies followed
in 2011.

00:02:01.875 --> 00:02:03.292
She played
the role of Kirsten

00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:05.792
in Jonathan Liebesman's
alien invasion sci-fi

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:07.125
Battle Los Angeles

00:02:07.208 --> 00:02:08.292
and she featured as Molly

00:02:08.375 --> 00:02:10.792
in Glenn Ficarra and John
Requa's romantic comedy

00:02:10.875 --> 00:02:12.125
Crazy, Stupid, Love

00:02:12.208 --> 00:02:13.875
as
Julianne Moore's daughter.

00:02:13.958 --> 00:02:16.333
She even found time
to appear in the music video

00:02:16.417 --> 00:02:17.708
for Taylor Swift's "Mean".

00:02:17.792 --> 00:02:20.458
But all you are is mean

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:22.833
In 2012,

00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:25.250
she landed her first
main role in a TV show

00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:26.708
as Charlie in Bent,

00:02:26.792 --> 00:02:29.000
an NBC sitcom
starring Amanda Peet,

00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:30.542
and she also featured
as Brianna

00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:32.292
in New Girl episode "Bully".

00:02:32.375 --> 00:02:34.208
Your happiness seems like
a mask.

00:02:34.292 --> 00:02:36.625
She got in her biggest film
to date the same year,

00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:38.333
playing
a young Talia al Ghul

00:02:38.417 --> 00:02:40.375
in Christopher Nolan's
third Batman film:

00:02:40.458 --> 00:02:41.750
The Dark Knight Rises.

00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:43.458
2013 turned out to be

00:02:43.542 --> 00:02:45.708
an especially busy
cinematic year for King.

00:02:45.792 --> 00:02:47.250
She played Christine Perron

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.750
in James Wan's
The Conjuring,

00:02:48.833 --> 00:02:50.167
one of five daughters
assailed

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.750
by supernatural forces

00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:53.833
in a sinister
Rhode Island farmhouse.

00:02:53.917 --> 00:02:56.167
Another voice role followed
in Sam Raimi's

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.417
Oz the Great and Powerful,

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.625
in which she played
the role of a living doll

00:02:59.708 --> 00:03:00.833
called China Girl.

00:03:00.917 --> 00:03:02.000
In 2014,

00:03:02.083 --> 00:03:04.083
King had a recurring role
as Greta Grimly,

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:06.667
the daughter of troubled
Duluth police deputy Gus

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.208
in critically acclaimed
crime drama Fargo.

00:03:09.292 --> 00:03:10.958
And she also had a role
in Zach Braff's

00:03:11.042 --> 00:03:11.917
Wish I Was Here,

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.458
a comedy drama
in which she plays Grace,

00:03:14.542 --> 00:03:17.458
the 12-year-old daughter
of Aidan and Sarah Bloom.

00:03:17.542 --> 00:03:19.208
More horror lurked
in the shadows

00:03:19.292 --> 00:03:21.333
with 2018's Slender Man,

00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:22.542
a Sylvain White film

00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:24.667
based on
the viral creepy pasta story

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.958
from the Something Awful
internet forum.

00:03:27.042 --> 00:03:28.958
King played the lead role
of Wren,

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.708
a Massachusetts girl
who makes the mistake of

00:03:30.792 --> 00:03:32.583
summoning
the eponymous monster.

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.417
A more cerebral
psychological horror role

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.625
followed in Veena Sud's
The Lie,

00:03:36.708 --> 00:03:39.750
a remake of 2015
German film We Monsters.

00:03:39.833 --> 00:03:41.542
King co-stars
as Kayla Logan,

00:03:42.125 --> 00:03:44.167
a girl who finds herself
trapped in a chilling lie

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.292
when her parents try to
cover up a fatal accident.

00:03:47.375 --> 00:03:49.875
King made
her Netflix debut in 2018

00:03:49.958 --> 00:03:51.375
with The Kissing Booth.

00:03:51.458 --> 00:03:52.917
King stars as Elle Evans,

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.208
a positive, quirky teenager

00:03:55.292 --> 00:03:56.958
whose budding romance
with bad boy Noah

00:03:57.042 --> 00:03:59.375
puts her lifelong friendship
with his younger brother Lee

00:03:59.458 --> 00:04:00.583
in peril.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.375
It's one of the most
re-watched films on Netflix,

00:04:03.458 --> 00:04:04.750
with one in three viewers

00:04:04.833 --> 00:04:06.583
diving back
in for another helping,

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:07.958
and it also bagged King

00:04:08.042 --> 00:04:09.625
a Favourite Actress
Kids' Choice Award

00:04:09.708 --> 00:04:11.167
for her portrayal of Elle.

00:04:13.458 --> 00:04:14.292
Oh no!

00:04:14.375 --> 00:04:17.250
King landed
two more TV roles in 2019.

00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:19.750
She appeared in three
episodes of Life In Pieces

00:04:19.833 --> 00:04:22.875
as Morgan, a pregnant
17 year old from Modesto,

00:04:22.958 --> 00:04:25.250
which also features
her older sister Hunter.

00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:26.500
And then she starred in

00:04:26.583 --> 00:04:28.625
award-winning
true crime drama The Act,

00:04:28.708 --> 00:04:31.333
based on the real-life case
of Gypsy Rose Blanchard.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.292
King plays Gypsy,
a chronically ill girl

00:04:34.375 --> 00:04:36.458
whose relationship with
her over-protective mother

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.667
takes a dark turn

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.208
when she learns
her illness was fabricated:

00:04:40.292 --> 00:04:42.792
a case of fictitious
disorder imposed on another

00:04:42.875 --> 00:04:44.417
or, as it's more
commonly known,

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.125
Munchausen's syndrome
by proxy.

00:04:46.208 --> 00:04:48.500
It was a critically
acclaimed performance

00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:50.625
and King was nominated
for an Emmy, Critics Choice

00:04:50.708 --> 00:04:51.958
and Golden Globe.

00:04:52.042 --> 00:04:54.708
2020 brought us a second
Kissing Booth movie

00:04:54.792 --> 00:04:56.750
in which King reprised
her role as Elle,

00:04:56.833 --> 00:04:58.458
and a third
and final instalment

00:04:58.542 --> 00:04:59.417
of the film trilogy

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.375
is available to watch
on Netflix now.

00:05:01.458 --> 00:05:03.708
Do you have a favourite
Joey King performance?

00:05:03.792 --> 00:05:06.083
How many times did you
re-watch The Kissing Booth?

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:07.500
Let us know in the comments

00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:09.583
and remember to subscribe to
the channel for more videos

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:12.542
about your favourite stars,
shows and movies.

